Verdict: NEED_MORE
Rationale: The claim has three material parts: (1) the home of the race is also the venue for the FIA Formula One Canadian Grand Prix, (2) it is home to the first Formula One race won by a black driver, and (3) the race featured Canadian drivers for the first time since 2006. The first part is supported by evidence identifying the venue as Circuit Gilles Villeneuve in Montreal. However, the second part is not supported, as no evidence identifies the first Formula One race won by a black driver or its venue. The third part is partially addressed, with evidence indicating Robert Kubica's 2008 Canadian Grand Prix appearance as the first post-2006 Canadian driver, but no further appearances are documented. Additional evidence is needed to confirm the second and third parts of the claim.
Rounds: 6, findings: 12
Sources:
- Canadian Grand Prix, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canadian_Grand_Prix
